        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Fix undo checkpoints",
        "summary": "Undo operations now restore `lastToolResults` alongside `agentState`. The `Checkpoint` interface includes a `lastToolResultsString` field. `CheckpointManager.addCheckpoint` accepts and serializes tool results. `Client.lastToolResults` visibility changed to public. CLI restore logic parses and applies the saved tool results.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T16:04:06.468Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you hit undo to go back to a previous step, your workspace now restores more faithfully, including the results from the last tools the assistant used, not just the assistant's state. Behind the scenes, the snapshot that gets saved now also records those latest tool results, the program that reads the workspace keeps track of them in a place other parts can reach, and the undo process loads them back in just like it already did for the assistant's state. This is internal housekeeping for how the assistant's memory of recent steps gets saved and restored, so there's nothing new on any screen to spot; it just makes stepping backward more reliable for anyone using that feature today.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "c22599ef5d04",
