      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Drop Gemini 2.5 Pro preview API fallback step",
        "summary": "Removes the direct Gemini API `gemini-2.5-pro-preview` attempt from `streamGemini25ProWithFallbacks`, shortening the chain to two Gemini exp steps, one OpenRouter preview step, and Claude Sonnet. Fallback logs now include `accumulatedContent` to aid debugging mid-stream failures. `main-prompt.ts` explicitly sets `temperature: 0` for the Gemini path.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T16:04:17.309Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "You won't notice anything different. Behind the scenes, the system tried to drop one of the backup routes it uses when asking the AI assistant for answers, but the actual flow of getting responses stays the same. Engineers adjusted how the assistant handles failures so they can see a bit more detail in their logs, and told one of the AI models to be less random in its answers. No new features or visible changes reach you from this update.",
